{"title":"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">2009 AMC 10B #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems\">2009 AMC 12B #11</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On Monday, Millie puts a quart of seeds, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of which are millet, into a bird feeder.  On each successive day she adds another quart of the same mix of seeds without removing any seeds that are left.  Each day the birds eat only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the millet in the feeder, but they eat all of the other seeds.  On which day, just after Millie has placed the seeds, will the birds find that more than half the seeds in the feeder are millet?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e8bbe5dcc18c8b53e23c4f4979f9a427c00da04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{Tuesday}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{Wednesday}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{Thursday}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{Friday}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{Saturday}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"625\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On Monday, day 1, the birds find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14d48fb052d7fa270cfe6d5a0b5ef1f1cb1c2ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> quart of millet in the feeder.  On Tuesday they find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c4050b4283bef8e8479cea9c214ea95a608e378a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac 14 + \\frac 34 \\cdot \\frac 14\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />\nquarts of millet.  On Wednesday, day 3, they find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4238653fc34a7f23ef0e4efcd926c173ee0c21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac 14 + \\frac 34 \\cdot \\frac 14 + \\left(\\frac34\\right)^2 \\cdot \\frac 14\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"46\" />\nquarts of millet.  The number of quarts of millet they find on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d743236100c927b7f7d555e4cb9fbd2deaa41520.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac 14 + \\frac 34 \\cdot \\frac 14 + \\left(\\frac34\\right)^2 \\cdot \\frac 14 + \\cdots + \\left(\\frac 34\\right)^{n-1} \\cdot \\frac 14 = \\frac {(\\frac 14)(1 - (\\frac 34)^n)}{1 - \\frac 34} = 1 - \\left(\\frac 34\\right)^n .\\]\" width=\"502\" height=\"48\" />\nThe birds always find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21715ef3fb94d12fc089969a648efb480cd5b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> quart of other seeds, so more than half the seeds are millet if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b584986ae0df9a125d12335f74c5d19a1877bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\left(\\frac 34\\right)^n &gt; \\frac 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"115\" height=\"44\" />, that is, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93d34b223c61801ea86f7dac9e5a28bae538194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac 34\\right)^n &lt; \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"44\" />.  Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a753d74be0fdd6c3a04c049d1fd316fe5763a7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac 34\\right)^4 = \\frac {81}{256} &gt; \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"141\" height=\"48\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86c0cace261a5fac8006ed6f3ada2a3c6c658cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac 34\\right)^5 = \\frac {243}{1024} &lt; \\frac 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"147\" height=\"46\" />, this will first occur on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a3462a48474f58c9f03792f3861279165d70485e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\text{Friday}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfbf4df7c25681bb178ddc50ee0c0d656aa25b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that, every day, there is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcb968f4f3d2e0d78a67fedc92a8d31183b2436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> quarts of other seeds in the feeder, so we simply need to calculate when the quantity of millet seeds is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcb968f4f3d2e0d78a67fedc92a8d31183b2436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> quarts. \nEvery day that elapses, a fourth of the millet is taken away (eaten by birds), and then a fourth of a quart is added (by Millie). Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> was the quantity of millet seeds the previous day, then on the next day, the quantity is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219f662f5f5e1f58ad838a7d2808493ce93c044c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac34n+\\dfrac14=\\dfrac14\\left(3n+1\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"175\" height=\"38\" /> \n<br />Monday: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f0ee320303ea164f9056db2442e2c6151f9acb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac14\\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"32\" height=\"38\" /><br /><br />\nTuesday: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb07423eddb9b628c81f10f5b318e58c915182d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac14\\left(3\\cdot\\dfrac14+1\\right)=\\dfrac{7}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"157\" height=\"45\" /><br /><br />\nWednesday: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/12146f37799ca37a471dca610dd779dd110dd2b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac14\\left(3\\cdot\\dfrac{7}{16}+1\\right)=\\dfrac{37}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"166\" height=\"45\" /><br /><br />\nThursday: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962fd9100529d177ae6d503c7626444a020e9f09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac14\\left(3\\cdot\\dfrac{37}{64}+1\\right)=\\dfrac{175}{256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" /><br /><br />\nFriday: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c3425ebfc21a524b0f8736753b53a8ede94052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac14\\left(3\\cdot\\dfrac{175}{256}+1\\right)=\\dfrac{781}{1024}&gt;\\dfrac{768}{1024}=\\dfrac34.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"300\" height=\"45\" /><br /><br />\nBrute forcing, we see that it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275145f0488aadd53b5e2eaddf1f0cf88b30083c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{Friday}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc93afd012d6af697c4fae71d14de49f021d78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />. \n~ aidan0626, lucaswujc, &amp; Technodoggo<br />\nNote: Yes there is a pattern to it, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c070db713fc383bf34d6446fd1877c4e8d3041ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"81\" height=\"46\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of days, as shown in Solution 1. This solution is only if you didn't notice the pattern. -aidan0626\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> denote the the amount of millet that the birds find on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> corresponds to Monday. Similarly, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> denote the amount of other seeds that the birds find on day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> satisfy the following:\n</p><p>\\begin{cases}\na_1=\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\na_n=\\frac{3}{4}a_{n-1}+\\frac{1}{4}\\quad (n&gt;1)\n\\end{cases}\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccea2e459edb19aa9a77a0458cb51cca418616c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_n=\\frac{3}{4}\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> using difference equations to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f71cc62180311c96026e09feec48ce59e177e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"141\" height=\"46\" />. We want to find the least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/b/d0b3d89eeafbc0cee05c6b145a15c6ace6afad82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&gt;\\frac{1}{2}(a_n+b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" />. In other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb4bdbfec746c03bf0920103c481d0d7b95159f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&gt;b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />. Substituting in what we know about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffd01cdc48042ce7c67d8edcd4904809831cfe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> we get:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312cd21e05980fffbfe0da6c05b028d25b8f0eaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^n+1&gt;\\frac{3}{4}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c0b4e97870e337450d94fd3614de7a44901dc40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^n&lt;\\frac{1}{4}\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b509677ea6bf3f5609ef8260a2eb397a1f7ff2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^n&lt;4^{n-1}\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4da30f8ab4ccb1d55203650a53b267802d6855a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n\\ge5\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nHence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275145f0488aadd53b5e2eaddf1f0cf88b30083c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{Friday}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc93afd012d6af697c4fae71d14de49f021d78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~tsun26\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jj3eCwD7Bms\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jj3eCwD7Bms</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B\">2009 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr